# Shell scripts are executed directly — as a Docker ENTRYPOINT, and as
# systemd ExecStart on a provisioned appliance. CRLF line endings break
# their shebang line ("#!/bin/sh\r" makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter that doesn't exist), surfacing as "no such file or
# directory" even though the file is genuinely there. Without this, a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the Git for Windows default)
# silently converts every one of these to CRLF and breaks them all.
*.sh text eol=lf
